mem-project_target_boost_tipin_coupling.inert_or_gated:
Target boost: the whole map path is bypassed when byte 0xFFFF5D03 == 0x5A, in which case the constant at 0x0C0C04 is used (value not shown). The map itself is not flat; it varies 243–1898, so it is not inert. Boost-Error comp: values 0.117–1.0 with no zero entries, so it is active. Tip-in enrichment is gated off (bit 7 of 0xFFFF7C5E cleared) when any of these holds:
- throttle change [0xFFFF62E4] < 'Minimum Tip-in Enrichment Activation (Throttle)' (0xCC4A0);
- the applied counter (0xFFFF7C5C) ≥ its ECT threshold (table A or B, chosen by 0xFFFF844F==1);
- byte 0xFFFF6254 ≠ 0, byte 0xFFFF726C ≠ 0, or byte 0xFFFF7D18 ≠ 0;
- the cumulative throttle (0xFFFF7C48) ≥ its ECT threshold (0xFFFF7C4C);
- the final product < 'Minimum Tip-in Enrichment Activation' (0xCC4A4).
If function 0x23E48 returns 0, ECT comp A is forced to 1.0. A negative throttle change zeroes the applied counter and the cumulative sum. The scalar threshold values are not in the pack.

mem-project_tipin_architecture.inert_or_gated:
Comp A (ECT) is all 1.0 and Comp D (ECT) is all 1.0, so both are inert multipliers. That also makes the Comp D decay in 0x03A8CC, the CC4A8=1.0 gate and the 0x23E48 gate irrelevant here. The A/B sets are functionally identical:
- Throttle Tip-in A = B;
- Comp B = Comp C;
- cumulative throttle limits A = B = 23.001;
- the applied-counter thresholds' bytes are not shown.
The 0xFFFF844F selector therefore has no effect, as far as the shown values go. Active gates: throttle increment >= 0.85, pulse >= 250, cumulative throttle < 23.001, applied count < table limit, and inhibit bytes 0xFFFF6254, 0xFFFF7D18 and 0xFFFF726C all 0. Both counter and cumulative resets occur after 22 calls with no shot.
